My current wizard, 11th level, is down on the 27th level of 
the dungeon.  His armor class is -3 and is wielding a +3 
Excalibur.  Up until the 24th level he had a very nice tamed 
cockatrice.  He hasn't come across one Thoth altar in his 
travels.  A ring of regeneration and a +1 ring of protection 
are on his fingers.  His luck was good at a fountain on 
about the fifth level when Excalibur was created. 
 
He, Borkus, has just come across a wand of wishing.  He 
wished for "a blessed +3 gray dragon scale mail".  What he 
got was -3 gray dragon scaled mail.   
 
Borkus came by his armor by polymorphing and then slaying a 
shopkeeper on an upper level.  Polypiling and examining.  
Nothing really wonderful. 
 
Things look kind of grim for Borkus.  Though he defeated a 
Golden Naga and a White Dragon, life is getting tough for a 
wizard who hasn't improved his armor class or weapon in more 
than a dozen levels. 
 
Metacommenting for a moment ... I've been playing Rogue, 
Hack, Larn, and NetHack for seven or eight years.  And I've 
certainly spent more time in 'it' than all the rest of the 
computer games I've ever played all put together.  In this 
notesfile, I see really amazing armor classes and frequently 
received wishes.  Either my luck or technique has been poor 
in these areas.  I would like suggestions. 


